    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.15685691085516237,
        "y0": 0.6707546434017143,
        "x1": 0.511953166886872,
        "y1": 0.6833337340692077
      },
      "text": "the first e edge of the next fundamental domain.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5225414201325062,
        "y0": 0.6707546434017143,
        "x1": 0.5623473622440512,
        "y1": 0.6833337340692077
      },
      "text": "Let T",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.5711710312787224,
        "y0": 0.6707546434017143,
        "x1": 0.8401906131918914,
        "y1": 0.6833337340692077
      },
      "text": "be the free splitting obtained from U",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.15685735964307598,
        "y0": 0.6859061585532295,
        "x1": 0.8419534521165237,
        "y1": 0.6984852492207229
      },
      "text": "by collapsing all edges labelled a, b, c, d, so T has a single natural edge orbit, represented by the",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1568567363265293,
        "y0": 0.7010576737047446,
        "x1": 0.5582287358302697,
        "y1": 0.713636764372238
      },
      "text": "T -image of any e-edge of U. Let α ⊂ T be the image of ˜",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.548425213184232,
        "y0": 0.7010576737047446,
        "x1": 0.8421499214920343,
        "y1": 0.713636764372238
      },
      "text": "α. Note that α crosses the unique natural",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.15685661166321999,
        "y0": 0.7160577954667987,
        "x1": 0.6613658331578074,
        "y1": 0.7286368861342921
      },
      "text": "edge orbit three times, the middle crossing being an interior crossing.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6711697547264348,
        "y0": 0.7160577954667987,
        "x1": 0.8419531529245813,
        "y1": 0.7286368861342921
      },
      "text": "Again α is contained in",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1568559135486877,
        "y0": 0.731209310618314,
        "x1": 0.8419540505004085,
        "y1": 0.7437884012858074
      },
      "text": "the axis of C in T, and α consists of one entire fundamental domain of that axis followed by the",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.15685596341401145,
        "y0": 0.746208931460525,
        "x1": 0.840779123742596,
        "y1": 0.7587880221280184
      },
      "text": "first edge of the next fundamental domain. Note that no two distinct translates of the axis of C",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.15685601327933518,
        "y0": 0.7613604466120402,
        "x1": 0.6180324180453431,
        "y1": 0.7739395372795337
      },
      "text": "have a common edge in T. It follows that the protocomponent β",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6180315204695159,
        "y0": 0.7687706375362897,
        "x1": 0.6299923167509192,
        "y1": 0.7775760034118036
      },
      "text": "Id",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6188159518771701,
        "y0": 0.7605887091521061,
        "x1": 0.6252865760154973,
        "y1": 0.7693940750276199
      },
      "text": "o",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.6307765985626022,
        "y0": 0.7613604466120402,
        "x1": 0.8421486249936172,
        "y1": 0.7739395372795337
      },
      "text": "(α) equals the axis of C in T,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.15685506583818423,
        "y0": 0.7765119617635554,
        "x1": 0.3054836497587316,
        "y1": 0.7890910524310488
      },
      "text": "and that C = Stab(β",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.30548275218290444,
        "y0": 0.7837707207660483,
        "x1": 0.31744352353164573,
        "y1": 0.7925760866415621
      },
      "text": "Id",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.30626656027401195,
        "y0": 0.7757402243036212,
        "x1": 0.3127371594796773,
        "y1": 0.7845455901791352
      },
      "text": "o",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.3182278552086525,
        "y0": 0.7765119424974075,
        "x1": 0.8419546738169552,
        "y1": 0.7890910331649009
      },
      "text": "(α)). But C has trivial image under abelianization of 〈a, b, c, d〉 and hence",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.15685631247127757,
        "y0": 0.7915120642594617,
        "x1": 0.842149422838797,
        "y1": 0.8040911549269552
      },
      "text": "C is not a free factor of 〈a, b, c, d〉. In fact we have the equation F[α; T] = {[〈a, b, c, d〉]}, in other",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.15685641220192503,
        "y0": 0.8066635794109769,
        "x1": 0.6766584807751226,
        "y1": 0.8192426700784703
      },
      "text": "words C fills the group 〈a, b, c, d〉, and hence α fills T by Proposition 2.9.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.18117029526654413,
        "y0": 0.821815094562492,
        "x1": 0.8419518564261642,
        "y1": 0.8343941852299854
      },
      "text": "The fact that C fills 〈a, b, c, d〉 can be proved using a beautiful transversality argument that",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1568563623366013,
        "y0": 0.8368152163245461,
        "x1": 0.8409740971583947,
        "y1": 0.8493943069920395
      },
      "text": "we learned from a paper of Stallings [Sta00]. Here are some details of this argument. Consider S",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.4911700479345384,
        "y0": 0.874542610813873,
        "x1": 0.5076406142290901,
        "y1": 0.8871217014813664
      },
      "text": "14",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
